-- A NAMED-FIELD VARIANT whose CONSTRUCTOR is spelled `Plain` — the same registry
-- key `plainlib`'s record `Plain` uses, but owned by type `Holder`.  That is what
-- makes key `Plain` collided in `universeRecordIdentsRef` with two candidates
-- whose OWNING TYPE NAMES differ, so an identity test that compares only the
-- declaring module (or only the key) cannot tell them apart.
--
-- `hxOf` projects `hx` HERE rather than in `entry`, on purpose: from `entry` the
-- receiver head is `Holder`, arm (a) misses, and the field→owners fallback resolves
-- `hx` through `pairRecordByName "Plain"` — a BARE-key read this unit deliberately
-- did NOT change (see the PR's "what this unit did not do").  Projecting inside the
-- declaring module keeps this cell about the paths unit 3 touches.
public export data Holder =
  | Plain { hx : Int }

export mkH : Holder
mkH = Plain { hx = 100 }

export hxOf : Holder -> Int
hxOf h = h.hx
